Hi Caroline and all,

Thanks for confirming this morning that both shifts on Trafford T2 and Warrin=
gton W1 are taking over the tagged-box handover from today. Gareth and Julie =
have T2, and Martin and Helen have W1, on mornings and evenings respectively.

Please take the old first-off instruction sheets off both lines by the end of=
 today and put the two-sided Rev 1 card at each bench. Gareth, please check t=
hat the old sheets have been collected on T2. Martin, please do the same on W=
1.

If a box of three first-off sheets is still on hold at shift change, leave th=
e tag attached and show the incoming lead what still needs checking. The rece=
iving lead records receipt, checks the sheets and tag against the job instruc=
tion and records the approval time when they match. Leave a box on the hold s=
helf if the tag is missing, the specification differs or approval is outstand=
ing. When the sheets actually go back into good stock, the receiving lead sig=
ns and records the actual return time separately.

From the week of 25 November, Gareth, please lead the open-tag checks on T2 w=
ith Julie, and Martin, please lead them on W1 with Helen. Match the open tags=
 to the boxes on the shelf and check what's holding up each release. The 17 O=
ctober T2 return remains unverified in the trial workbook. Keep that historic=
al gap separate from the list of boxes currently on hold.

I've attached Siobhan's handover briefing for circulation, Connor's ticket an=
d weight tie-out, and Caroline's issued bench card (MCP-OPS-QRC-2024-001 Rev =
1), which takes effect today.

Thanks,
Nicholas

